From e5fa8fd2716d5cb2caa953f4da9a6d487eb23b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuuuuuuuuhvt <107742395+Yuuuuuuuuhvt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:26:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tabs): open tab config links in the background

Add `activate` and `placement` query parameters to
`warp://tab_config/<name>` links. `activate=false` inserts the tab
without switching to it, so the tab the user is typing in keeps
keyboard focus; `placement` overrides the `new_tab_placement` setting
for that tab. Unknown values are rejected so a typo cannot fall back to
a focus-stealing tab.

While Warp is in the background there is no active window, and the
primary window fallback may not host a workspace. Tab config links now
pick the frontmost window that has a workspace before opening a new
window, which previously failed with "no workspace available".

Refs warpdotdev/warp#16256

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
